{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno3_js_upwind_D1x",
    "description": "Pointwise third-order Jiang-Shu WENO3 upwind derivative d u/dx at the cell (i, j) of cartesian_uniform_2d: stencils/weno3_js_upwind_D1 bound to the five cells u at offsets -2..+2 along x and spacing dx, with the upwind side chosen by the sign of the supplied selector sgn (sgn >= 0 takes the left-biased reconstruction, sgn < 0 its mirror image, as in fire_behavior's Select_weno3). fire_behavior's Select_weno3 (dx, lfn(i, j), ..., signo_x). u is the field, i and j the cell indices, bound by the caller's faq; sgn is an expression the caller forms at (i, j) -- the wind-relative sign (stencils/grad4_dot_wind times stencils/central_D1x_4_point) in fire_upwinding = 8. It reaches two cells either side along x, so a caller evaluates it only on the block where that fits. The one spelling of the WENO3 branch along x; the third-order sibling of stencils/weno5_js_upwind_D1x.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "axes:x",
      "order:3",
      "stencil_width:5"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P. A., & Coen, J. L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 10(4), 908-926. The hybrid WENO/ENO1 level-set schemes (fire_upwinding = 8, 9) of WRF-Fire / NCAR fire_behavior.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls (case 8), Select_eno, Select_weno3, Select_4th, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "weno3_js_upwind_D1.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno3_js_upwind_D1x": {
      "params": [
        "u",
        "i",
        "j",
        "sgn"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "weno3_js_upwind_D1",
        "bindings": {
          "h": "dx",
          "m2": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "u",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "i",
                  2
                ]
              },
              "j"
            ]
          },
          "m1": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "u",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "i",
                  1
                ]
              },
              "j"
            ]
          },
          "c": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "u",
              "i",
              "j"
            ]
          },
          "p1": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "u",
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "i",
                  1
                ]
              },
              "j"
            ]
          },
          "p2": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "u",
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "i",
                  2
                ]
              },
              "j"
            ]
          },
          "sgn": "sgn"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
